From: Holodor <holodor@transentient.github.io>
Date: Tue, 12 Aug 2026 18:20:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: mux: wcd939x-usbss: park in audio mode when Type-C idle

The AYN Odin 3 routes its integrated 3.5mm jack through the WCD939x USBSS
analog switch.  MBHC mechanical detection needs the jack's lines connected
to the codec, but the switch powers up (and returns to, on every Type-C
detach) USB routing, where the lines float and insertion can never be
seen.  ROCKNIX's 0063 routes the switch to audio *after* a mech-detect
interrupt -- which on this board can never fire first (chicken-and-egg;
proven on hardware 2026-08-12: MBHC armed 0x3014=0xBD, zero interrupts
ever, manual switch programming + MBHC re-arm = detection works).

Park the switch in audio-accessory routing whenever the Type-C state is
SAFE (probe already ends in a SAFE set, so this also covers boot).  Any
genuine USB/DP mode still overrides while a partner is attached.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c
@@ -390,8 +390,18 @@
 	bool enable_dp = false;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Idle/safe: park the switch in audio-accessory routing.  On boards
+	 * with an integrated 3.5mm jack wired through this switch (AYN
+	 * Odin 3), the jack's HPHL/HPHR and mech-detect lines float while
+	 * the switch sits in USB routing, so the codec's MBHC can never see
+	 * an insertion.  Parking in audio arms jack detection whenever no
+	 * Type-C partner claims the port; any real mode below overrides.
+	 */
+	if (usbss->mode == TYPEC_STATE_SAFE) {
+		enable_audio = true;
 	/* USB Mode */
-	if (usbss->mode < TYPEC_STATE_MODAL ||
+	} else if (usbss->mode < TYPEC_STATE_MODAL ||
 	    (!usbss->svid && (usbss->mode == TYPEC_MODE_USB2 ||
 			      usbss->mode == TYPEC_MODE_USB3))) {
 		enable_usb = true;
